# Let a keyboard behind the Dell dock wake the machine from suspend.
#
# The keyboard itself is wake-capable, but a USB wake signal has to travel up
# through every hub above it, and the dock's hubs default to wakeup=disabled:
#
#   HP Elite USB Keyboard   enabled
#   Dell dock hub 5-2.3     disabled   <- signal stops here
#   Dell dock hub 5-2       disabled
#
# So docked with the lid shut there was no way to resume: the internal keyboard
# is out of reach and the power button is bound to poweroff.
#
# Matched on the product string rather than the bus path, because the path
# (5-2, 5-2.3) changes with which port the dock is plugged into. The dock
# presents four hubs, two per USB bus, and all of them need this.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{bDeviceClass}=="09", ATTR{product}=="Dell dock", ATTR{power/wakeup}="enabled"
